  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SDG Development Plans developed</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. PMU is fully functional in the Planning department of Uttarakhand to operate CPPGG to localize SDGs
2. Enhance SDG Integration and Localisation through monitoring and evalaution to incease awareness around SDGs
3. Capacity Building of new and existing staff, youth and urban local bodies to increase awareness and advocacy on SDGs.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. A training program was organized at ATI Nainital for state government officers of Urban Local Bodies on SDGs.

2. SDG sensitization workshops in colleges and schools have been organized at block levels. In the first phase students, orientation was done and ICT materials have been distributed. In the second phase, quiz competitions, poster-making, and speech competitions will be conducted.

3. As per the revised format, introduced by the MoPR, GoI, for the preparation of GPDP, two training programme have been conducted for capacity building of the District level master trainers.

4.Two national workshops organized by MoPR, GoI, atattendedy the ACEP-CPPGG and SDG Localization Expert.

5. Signature campaigns and workshops were conducted on SDG 7thAnniversary, in all the districts and at the state level. Poster-making, SDG quiz competitions, and other events were also organized at the school level in all the districts.

6. SDG Anniversary was celebrated at the Secretariat, GoUK as a part of the advocacy and communication campaign of SDGs 

7. Monitoring framework manual developed. It includes indicators on gender and in SDG 5 (Gender Equality).

8. SDG index district profiles developed and is in the process of dissemination to the districts. 

9. Data validation protocol manual development.

10. Quarterly Newsletter Nitighosh Vol 1, Issue- 6 June-July 2022, Published and circulated.

11. Factsheet 1- Uttarakhand status on India Innovation Index 2021 published and circulated.

12. Policy brief on declining female labour force participation in Uttarakhand published.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Establish PMU to support the development of action plans, proposals and policies for enhancing state economic growth                            
2. Strengthen capacities of government officials on implementation and localisation of SDGs                                                  3. Develop vision 2030 documents for achieving SDGs for 13 districts                                       4. Disseminate information amongst stakeholders on SDGs and their role in implementing SDGs at district level</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Established PMU in the Centre for Public Policy and Good Governance with six sector specific experts
2. Organized workshops and stakeholder consultations in 13 districts</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Enhance the capacity of the CPPGG PMU in State level Plannnng and SDG integration &amp; Localisation
2. PMU of CPPGG is fully finctional
3. Capacity building of new and existing staff and, knowledge management</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. SDG Consultation workshops conducted in all districts 
2. SDG district vision plan, prepared for all districts 
3. SDG sensitization workshops, conducted in all 13 districts 
4. Placement of 7 consultants in PMU of CPPGG, completed. 
5. Development of a &#x2018;Talk on SDGs&#x2019; series for familiarizing the staff with the objectives of all SDGs. 
6. District level monthly monitoring indicator framework, finalised.
7. Institutionalisation of the district wise SDG monitoring dashboard.
8. Development of SDG Gram Panchayat Development Plan (GPDM), SDG Integration manual.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
